# The pack payload is a BUILD artifact (4.2 F4): tools/build_asset_packs.py build assembles the
# four SoC #group_ variants here from the measured vendor zips, every byte hash-verified against
# the census on the way in and out. The vendor-licensed model binaries must never enter a repo
# with a public remote, and the root .gitignore's blob walls (*.so, *.dlc, *.context) do not
# cover .bin — so this pattern IS the wall. The default variant's .gitkeep stays tracked; the
# payload dirs are structurally uncommittable.
#
# (4.2 F8) The directory is named after the PACK, not "model". Both modules used to write
# assets/model#group_<g>/, and every entry under it therefore had a twin at the same path in the
# sibling module — which bundletool's EntryClashValidator refuses outright when the content
# differs ("Modules 'npu_small' and 'npu_turbo' contain entry
# 'assets/model#group_soc_7gen4/metadata.json' with different content"). The bins escaped it only
# because turbo's carry the turbo_ prefix; metadata.json did not, and the FIRST bundleRelease
# ever attempted failed on it. Naming the directory after the pack makes the whole clash class
# impossible instead of fixing the one instance.
#
# (4.2 F8) The pattern stops at `soc_` DELIBERATELY. The EMPTY default variant is no longer an
# unsuffixed sibling — bundletool refuses that outright ("Directory 'assets/npu_turbo' must have
# exactly one device group, but found []") — it is the explicit `#group_other` variant, and its
# .gitkeep is TRACKED. Every census packGroup begins `soc_`, so `#group_soc_*` is exactly the
# four payload dirs and exactly nothing else; a wider `#group_*` would swallow the one directory
# in this module that must stay visible to git.
src/main/assets/npu_turbo#group_soc_*/
